{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfbuf1rxcaXMFQfhvC9TP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags here are simple and file-based. I checked the code and it matches the project's stored convention.\n\n**How it works** (`src/flags.py`):\n- Every flag is declared in `flags.toml` under `[flags]`. Right now the only one is `invoice-pdf-v2 = false`.\n- Code checks a flag with `flags.is_on(\"name\")`. `all_flags()` returns a copy of all of them.\n- Flag names are kebab-case.\n\n**Adding your checkout flag:**\n\n1. Declare it in `flags.toml`, off by default:\n   ```toml\n   [flags]\n   invoice-pdf-v2 = false\n   new-checkout = false\n   ```\n2. Branch on it in `src/api/checkout.py`:\n   ```python\n   from src import flags\n\n   @bp.post(\"/checkout\")\n   def checkout():\n       if flags.is_on(\"new-checkout\"):\n           return _new_checkout()\n       ...existing flow...\n   ```\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **A typo won't raise an error.** `is_on()` returns `False` for any name that isn't declared, so a misspelled name just leaves the new flow off. Double-check the name matches `flags.toml` exactly.\n- **Flags are read once, when the module is imported.** Changing `flags.toml` needs a process restart. There's no environment-variable override and no per-user or percentage rollout. The flag is either on for everyone or off for everyone. If you need a gradual rollout, the flag system itself would have to be extended.\n- **Nothing calls `is_on()` yet**, so your checkout flag would be the first real use in the codebase.\n\nWant me to wire it up?"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 333, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25843, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 333}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}